  "context_pill": "Section 10(10BC) - Disaster Compensation Exemption",
  "example_summary": "Compensation of ₹ 5,00,000 paid by the Government of Chhattisgarh to Amit's parents following the Dantewada bus bomb blast is fully exempt under Section 10(10BC).",
  "source_provision": "| Statutory Provision | Governing Authority | Eligible Payers | Tax Treatment |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| Section 10(10BC) | Disaster Management Act, 2005 | Central Government, State Government, Local Authority | 100% Exempt from Tax |\n\n\n> [!IMPORTANT]\n> Definition of Disaster: A catastrophe, mishap, calamity, or grave occurrence arising from natural or man-made causes, accident, or negligence, causing substantial loss of life or human suffering beyond the coping capacity of the affected community.\n\n\n> [!WARNING]\n> Exemption Limit: There is no upper monetary ceiling prescribed under Section 10(10BC); the entire compensation received from the specified governmental authorities is fully exempt.",
